1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.snl.no/.nbl_biografi/Jens_Pederss%C3%B8n_Skielderup/utdypning
2 CONT  Born 1484  Skjelderup  Jylland
2 CONT
2 CONT Skrevet om hendes søn: Ingenting er kjent om Jens Skielderups bakgrunn og oppvekst. Albert Hatting [skrev i sin "Forsøg til en Præste-Historie" (Bergen 1774 / København 1775) at han] mente han var født 1499 på Fyn av foreldrene Pe
2 CONC der Jensen og Maren Nielsdatter, Gerhard Schøning at han var fra Jylland og at faren var bonde, moren landflyktig fra Holland. Han var nok født et stykke inn på 1500-tallet, og ut fra Absalon Pederssøns dagbok kan man slutte at ha
2 CONC n var fra Jylland
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde: Finn Holbek: www.finnholbek.dk: Peder Jensen og hans kone Maren Nielsdatter døde begge hos deres søn biskop Jens Pedersen Skjelderup i Bergen i Norge. Johan Reppe skriver i sin håndskrevne stamtavle at Peder Jensen "opgis å
2 CONC  være født 1454, død 1564", altså ble han 110 år gammel.
2 CONT
2 CONT English Born 1484 Skjelderup Jutland Written about her son: Nothing is known about Jens Skielderup's background and upbringing. Albert Hatting [wrote in his 'Attempt to a Priesthood Story' (Bergen 1774 / Copenhagen 1775) that he b
2 CONC elieved that he was born in 1499 on Funen by Peder Jensen and Maren Nielsdatter, Gerhard Schøning, that he was from Jutland and that his father was farmer, mother, fugitive from Holland. He was born a little in the 16th century, a
2 CONC nd from the diary of Absalon Pedersson, one can conclude that he was from Jutland
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Find Holbek: www.finnholbek.dk: Peder Jensen and his wife Maren Nielsdatter both died at their son Bishop Jens Pedersen Skjelderup in Bergen, Norway. Johan Reppe writes in his handwritten pedigree that Peder Jensen 'was ra
2 CONC ised to be born 1454, dead 1564', so he became 110 years old.
