1 OCCU Dr.med.og læge, erster Arzt in Lübeck, Enkedronning Dorotheas livlege, "Medicinæ Doctor & Professor Physices" i Lübeck., professor i Lübeck, Doctor læge i Gent
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://xn--slgtensspor-b9a.dk/index.php/2022/11/07/hieronymus-knopf-og-barbara-von-der-rhone-paludan/
2 CONT
2 CONT Også kalt Johan van den Broeck (senere latinifisert etternavn til Paludan). Født i Gent i Oost-Flanderen i
2 CONT
2 CONT Belgia. Livlege hos enkedronning Dorothea. Døde i Lübeck, Tyskland.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Enkedronning Dorotheas livlege.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde: nermo.org
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.multimodis.no/Slekt/642.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.martander.dk/28215725
2 CONT
2 CONT According to a handwritten genealogy from 1769, he was born in Gent, Flanders, in 1479. He was a doctor there and became a protestant. For this, he was thrown in prison by the Duke of Alba. But the duke became ill, and Dr. Paludan
2 CONC  was able to help him. As a reward, he was allowed to emigrate with his family, and he settled as doctor in Luebeck, where he died in 1561. 2
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Conflict on death date--will check other sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT The record of his  enrolled at the Medical University of Montpellier as a man who came from the district or the city Aalst in East Flanders.  His name was originally “Van den Broeck.”   The family tradition has him coming from Gen
2 CONC t—two villages with the same name may have been mixed up in the medical school records.   There is also a possibility that he was a brother of Nicholas Buscoducensis 
2 CONT
2 CONT The medical school quote is as follows:  "1528: 883rd Paludanus Joannes, Alostensis, dioctyl Cameracensis. (Schyron) 13 Janvier".   This means:  “Hans Paludan came from the city or country Aalst in Cambrai pin in present Belgium. 
2 CONC He was on 13.1.1528 enrolled at Montpellier University medical school, probably the doctor Schyron. “  Years later, a son, Joannes Paludanus, also enrolled at the same medical school.,  
2 CONT
2 CONT  After becoming a protestant, he emigrated to Lübeck with his family.   A family legend says he was thrown in prison by the Duke of Alba, whom he cured.  Other sources question this because the dates do not agree.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Other biographical information is available online.  Hans Paludan, 1538-1615 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.munthe.net/database/g0002053.html#I8024
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogy.munthe.net/database/g0002785.html#I39411
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Også kalt Johan van den Broeck (senere latinifisert etternavn til Paludan). Født i Gent i Oost-Flanderen i
2 CONT
2 CONT Belgia. Livlege hos enkedronning Dorothea. Døde i Lübeck, Tyskland.
