1 OCCU 1724 til Bjørnsholm. Adlet, 1713 paa Bjørnsholm
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anders_Kj%C3%A6rulf
2 CONT
2 CONT 1662-1725 Anders Mortensen Kiærulf til øen Fuur, Bjørnsholm, Ørndrup (og Rakkeby Kirche), Sødal og Holmegård var først forpagter på Gudumlund og Lindenborg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Han fik meget gods og 1724 blev han adlet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Med Kirstine Møller fik han 3 børn.  eller  10 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1687 -1728 var Bjørnsholm ejet af Anders Mortensen Kjærulf. (Nygaards sedler)
2 CONT *  12. november 1695 kgl. res., at Anders Kjærulf maa underlægge Bjørnsholm hovedgaard 1 bol i Ranum by mod at betale 50 rdlr. og svare skatterne for det løbende aar (rigsark. uddarg af kgl. res. (Nygaards sedler)
2 CONT *  1700 Aug 9th reference: December 1700 Morsø Nørre-Morsø Sønder Herredsfoged: Justitsprotokol [https://www.sa.dk/ao-soegesider/da/billedviser?epid=17142559#299426,61620221]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1702 Bjørnsholm 51-3-3-.- ejet af Anders Kjærulf. (Nygaards sedler)
2 CONT *  1710 var Bjørnsholm beboet af Anders Kjæruls med kone (Nygaards sedler).
2 CONT
2 CONT *  2. marts 1711 fik Anders Kjærulf på Bjørnsholm og hans kone Kirsten Pedersdatter Møller kgl. bev. på at denlængstlevende maatte sidde i uskiftet bo med fælles umyndige børn (Jy.reg. 24.30, nr.35 ) (Nygaards sedler) 
2 CONT
2 CONT *  25. november 1712 skøde fra kongen til AndersKjærulf på Flejsborg og Hyllerberg kirke (Nygaardssedler)
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1718 Anders Kjærulf på Bjrønsholm,Mølgaard og Ørndrup 360 Øxner (Nygaards sedler)
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1724 blev Anders Mortensen Kjærulf til Fur adlet.
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1728 -30 var Bjørnsholm ejet Anders Mortensen søn Søren Kjærulf (Nygaards sedler)
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1729 -1735: Anders Kjærulf, der ejede Sødal fra 1729 til sin død i 1735, var søn af herredsfoged Morten Laursen i Kjær Herred. Han var en hård mand, der havde samlet sig en masse gods og efter sigende ikke altid på en lige hæde
2 CONC rlig måde. Kjærulf ejede bl.a. Bjørnsholm (Vitskøl Kloster), Ørndrup på Mors, Holmgaard i Skals med flere gårde. Han blev i 1724 optaget i adelsstanden. Hans første kone, Kristine Møller, døde i 1725, hvorefter han i 1728 giftede 
2 CONC sig med den 30 år yngre Margrethe Dorthea Braes, der var datter af Kalundborgs borgmester Diderik Christian Braes, som ejede godset Kokkedal. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Kjærulf s ægteskab med Dorthea Braes varede imidlertid kun syv år, da Kjærulf døde i 1735 og hans enke forpagtede nu Sødal ud til Didrek Iversen, der havde været ridefoged på gården siden 1732. Om denne forpagtning, der var på meg
2 CONC et favorable vilkår, er der meget sparsomme oplysninger, men det synes som om han har haft gården uden nogen egentlig forpagtningsafgift. Efter fru Braes' død blev det i hvert fald til retsforfølgning vedrørende forpagtningen, ide
2 CONC t hendes far ville bestride gyldigheden af de alt for gode vilkår, han havde haft gården på. At grunden til forholdet muligvis har været et påtænkt ægteskab mellem ejerinden og forpagteren, er en anden sag. Margrethe Dorthea Braes
2 CONC  døde imidlertid i 1740, men forinden havde hun betænkt sine sognebørn ved at oprette herredets første skoler. http://www.rodding-borger.dk/index.php/lokalhistorie/sodal/84-herremaend-fra-sodal-satte-praeg-pa-egnen
2 CONT
2 CONT *  1733 var Anders Kierulf til Søby kurator for sin bror Laurs' børnebørn Johannes og Thomas i forbindelse med deres kongelige tilladelse til at være egen værge. (Nygaards sedler)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not known what happened to Niels Juul later, but already in 1668 his father-in-law Axel Juul of Volstrup (Hjerm parish) had let himself enter in his main farm Gunderupgård with estate and some land from Bjørnsholm's estate. 
2 CONC He, (+1671) or his widow fru Elisabeth Friis, must later also have been the owner of Bjørnsholm, which she shortly before her death (1677) willed to her daughter Ingeborg Juul's 10 children with Tyge Below, but they were in 1686 a
2 CONC llowed by royal permission to sell it, since it could not unravel the taxes. In 1689 they conveyed the farm to Anders Mortensen Kjærulf, and then the farm came into safer conditions. It was high time, if the the estate should be p
2 CONC revented from being a ruin.
2 CONT
2 CONT There was enough to do for Anders Kjærulf; he was a son of a herredsfoged in Kær herred and had been a manager of several manors - and he very much extended the added estate of the farm and achieved several tiender (taxes). He est
2 CONC ablished the farm Lundgård, and a far away placed farm Padkær came also in existence - it laterbecame an impressive property. He bought five other manors. It was said about him after his death that he had "scraped togethere much e
2 CONC state and means", but it was added " not quite fair, for he was a hard man to deal with". He managed Bjørnsholm himself, of course by villeinage, and therefore the domestic staff at his farm was small. He was a great bullock-breed
2 CONC er - in 1718 he had 360 bullocks in his stables. Although he was not a "fin" (noble) man, he achieved in 1724 to be enobled together with his brother Laurids of Wiffertsholm.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Kjærulf died at Sødal in 1735, but he had already exchanged property with his only living son, regimentskvartermester (military title) Søren Kjærulf, since he had got married again. The son got Bjørnsholm, Ørndrup at the is
2 CONC land Mors and Halkær, which together had a value of ab. 60.000 rigsdaler. He lived at Halkær and died there already two years later. He succeeded in losing everything, and his widow pawned in 1731 Bjørnsholm estate to her mother's
2 CONC  brother Peder Thøgersen Lassen of Rødslev (+ 1737), who the same year was enobled in the name Lasson - and who the following year became its owner. In the exchange after him it was transferred together with Sønder Vosborg to his 
2 CONC son Mathias Lasson, who later became the owner of several important manors. He extended the adjoining estate of Bjørnsholm and bought several tiender (taxes) and became the owner of the church, which was built together with Bjørns
2 CONC holm. His name is especially attached to the manor, since he built or rebuilt the eastern wing, partly upon old foundations and with the medieval walls.
