1 OCCU regimentskvartermester, kancelliråd- 1728 til 1730 ejer af Bjørnsholm
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anders Kjærulf died at Sødal in 1735, [but he had already exchanged property with his only living son, regimentskvartermester (military title) Søren Kjærulf, since he had got married again. The son got Bjørnsholm, 
2 CONC Ørndrup at the island Mors and Halkær, which together had a value of ab. 60.000 rigsdaler. He lived at Halkær and died there already two years later. He succeeded in losing everything, and his widow pawned in 1731 Bjørnsholm estat
2 CONC e to her mother's brother Peder Thøgersen Lassen of Rødslev (+ 1737), who the same year was enobled in the name Lasson - and who the following year became its owner. In the exchange after him it was transferred together with Sønde
2 CONC r Vosborg to his son Mathias Lasson, who later became the owner of several important manors. He extended the adjoining estate of Bjørnsholm and bought several tiender (taxes) and became the owner of the church, which was built tog
2 CONC ether with Bjørnsholm. His name is especially attached to the manor, since he built o]r rebuilt the eastern wing, partly upon old foundations and with the medieval walls.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thyrashm.blogspot.dk/2010/05/vitskl-klosterbjrnsholm-himmerland.html
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://archive.org/stream/ViborgKatedralskolesDimittender/Viborg%20Katedralskoles%20Dimittender_djvu.txt] 29. Søren Andersen Kjærulf. Søn al godsejer A. Mortensen K. og Kirstine Pedersdatter Møller. F. 1693, godsejer, regimentsk
2 CONC vartermester og auditør i Ålborg, f 18/8 1730. G. m. Johanne Marie Benzon, tf. 28/2 1707 på Juellinge, f 3-4/9 1776 i Ålborg (Klitgaard: Kjærulf ske Studier, 164). 
