2 ADDR
1 OCCU f. Thisted/Danmark døpt 1692 i Kristiansand, borger av Kristiansand i 1717 (Borgerrulle for Kristiansand 1641-18290) Borgerbrev i Skien 1722 som urmaker og gullsmed. Oppgav da at han var født i Thisted, Danmark., Lensmann
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Lårsdal Soga by Olav T. Bakken, pages 568-569:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Comment-Much is told and writen on Mickel Mandt. So much that we got perplexed to try to find out the most likely on what which was true on this man, and what was imagination. They were so special that the time prior to when they
2 CONC  went to Vinje, gave fertile soil for stories and adventure. We now have to manage to find one's way in archives and books, which will maybe take some of adventure from him, but there is still much left:
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikkel Mandt was a citizen of Kristiansand in 1717. On Feb. 5, 1722 he was listed as citizen at Skien as a goldsmith and watchmaker. He is listed as born in Thisted, Denmark.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Kristiansand's "Mandtal for Kop-, Heste of Ildstedsskatt" for the year 1700 is listed, Lauridtz Manth, Goldsmith. In 1698 is listed "Lauridtz Goldsmith." In 1697 - Lars Goldsmith. This leads us to believe that the father to Mic
2 CONC kel moved from Thisted to Kristiansand. Then Mickel came to Norway as little boy."
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikkel Mandt was born and baptized in Denmark. He grew up in Kristiansand, Norway. Then he went to Skien, Norway and ended up in Vinje, Telemark, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Lårsdal Soga by Olav T. Bakken, pages 225:
2 CONT
2 CONT "One can safely say on Mandt family, that is it full of descendants in every nook and cranny. Friends you talk with in the western districts say they have the family roots back to the old Mandt, Mikkel Larssen, born in1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikkel was a sivlersmith of pipes (musical), but in addition a versatile fellow according to record in Kalls book for Mo. "He was prominent in all places, citizen and goldsmith in Kristiansand, petty officer with the first Western
2 CONC  lands regiment, sheriff in Vinje, then sexton in same place, at last died peacefully without holding any office at his son Petter's farm at North Omblie.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mikkel and Else had 7 children: Lars Laurentius, Ingebreth, Rasmus, Olav, Peter Christian, Johanne Elisebeth and Gjertrud."
2 CONT
2 CONT References/sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial - Curch book for Mo sogn (parish) in Fyresdal prgj. - (4. aug.) http://urn.digitalarkivet.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20061214340104.jpg
