1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rasmus Mickelsen Mandt, * 1729, † 1813 i Mo, Telemark. 2 †r mellom f›dsels og d›psdag. Kilde
2 CONT
2 CONT Olav Mandt og Halvor Olav Mandt oppgir d›ds†r til 1815, mens Halvor Nordb› oppgir Br›drene Rasmus
2 CONT
2 CONT og Olav (Ole) var i tillegg til Peter ogs† De ble i 1782 anklaget for aa v‘re "fuskere" av guldsmedene
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Cudrio Levin i Skien. "Amtet" besluttet 14.3.1782 aa staar det i Christianiagullsmedenes
2 CONT
2 CONT laugsprotokoll. Han giftet seg med (1) Tårånn Mo Midjås. Tårånn: Ragnhild Pr›ytz opererer med Mikkel
2 CONT
2 CONT som s0nn - TH regner han ekteskap. Han giftet seg med (2) Gunhild Olsdatter Haatveit. Gunhild: 10 barn.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 gutter og 4 piker.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT •Residence: BET. 1755 - 1786 Farmed Søndre Midjås  •Residence: 1788 He moved to a farm called Nedrebø  •Burial: Mo Churchyard, Telemark, Noreay  •_FA2: He was the first to grow potatoes in Norway  •_FA3: 1781 He shot a bear  •_FA3
2 CONC : Awarded a gold medal by the Danish Agricultural Soc.  •Note:  Mo Bygdebok, Gard og ætt, Vol. I, Mo sokn, page 366.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rasmus Mandt was born on Skjelvik in Vinje and married the first time with Torunnn Aslaksdatter N. Midås (1729- ). After she died he married Gunhild Olavsdatter (1741-1813) from Upper Håtveit. He was a fine silversmith. Together w
2 CONC ith the brother Ingebret Resen was he the first in Norway to grow potatoes. He got a Silver medal from Landhusholdingselskapet (Danish Agricultural Society) for breaking new lands. After his son Olav took over the farm in 1788, Ra
2 CONC smus and wife moved to Nedrebø and lived there the rest on their lives.
