1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Lårsdal Soga by Olav T. Bakken, pages 569:
2 CONT
2 CONT "In Thisted, Denmark church book we find under 1692 - On April 15, Lauritz Rasmussøn Guldsmieds and Engel Mickeldatters baptized their child Mickel."
2 CONT
2 CONT Accoring to the above records, Lauritz (or Lars) was in Denmark in 1692 and he was a goldsmith. It not know where he was born or came from before Thisted. About 1697 he came to Kristiansand, Norway. It is not known when or where h
2 CONC e died, but probably in Kristiansand.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Lårsdal Soga by Olav T. Bakken, page 225:
2 CONT
2 CONT It is not wholly clear, the place of origination (or the Mandt family), but likely it was of german ancestry. Many differently stories tells (us) that Lauritz came to this land as a fugitive and was a friend with Else Larssen Rese
2 CONC n, shopman's daughter in Halden.
