1 NOTE He was named as Parish Priest and Dean in Roskilde Cathedral on June 23, 1627. He served as a 
2 CONT teacher (Informator) of Prince Frederik in 1649; he was the tutor of the children of King Christian IV and 
2 CONT Kristine Munk, including Leonora Christina. He had a stroke in 1658 and preached from a sitting position 
2 CONT
2 CONT from then on. He was offered the bishoprics of Stavanger in 1661 and Bergen in 1665, but elected to 
2 CONT remain in Roskilde.
